"""
AI Conscious Battery Optimizer — Kivy prototype
--------------------------------------------------
Native port of the web mockup: three radial gauges (Resistance / Heat / Cool)
with glowing status color, static green/yellow/red zone rings, an overheat
banner, a high-resistance shutdown/restart sequence, a "This device" vs
"Bluetooth device" source toggle, an F/C unit toggle, AI auto-correct behind
a hard safety lock, and a Structural Risk Index readout adapted from
R = w_e*e + w_u*u + w_r*(1-r) + w_m*(1-m).

Drop this in as main.py next to your existing buildozer.spec
(requirements = python3,kivy already covers everything here — no extra
dependencies needed). Bluetooth is a UI-level stub: swap scan_devices() /
connect_to() for a real BLE library (e.g. plyer, or a custom
python-for-android recipe) when you wire up actual hardware — the safety
lock (auto-correct can nudge, never override manual shutoff) should stay
enforced in that layer too, not just in the UI.
"""

